I walk up the stairs.
I have two bags in my hands.
I am finally at my new door.
I have a key in my pocket.
I put the bags down on the floor.
I take out the key.
I unlock the door.
I push the door open and go inside.
The apartment is small, but it is perfect.
It has nice, light furniture.
I look into the living room.
There is a sofa standing by the window.
There is a rug under the sofa.
There is a small cushion lying on the sofa.
There is a lamp standing in the corner.
Everything is ready for me.
I smile broadly.
It is my first real home in Copenhagen.
